# Build context for backend/Dockerfile. It sits at the MONOREPO ROOT, not in
# backend/, because that is where the context is rooted (see backend/Dockerfile
# for why the context stays at Code/ now that the backend no longer reaches
# outside its own directory).
#
# Kept deliberately general rather than "exclude everything but backend/": the
# excluded paths are the ones that are heavy, secret, or host-specific, so a
# future frontend image can share this file instead of fighting it. A
# Dockerfile that wants something different can drop its own
# <name>.Dockerfile.dockerignore beside itself, which takes precedence.

# Dependency trees. These are the expensive ones -- without this line the
# context upload alone is several GB, and any host-built native binary in here
# (bcrypt, the Windows Prisma engine) is wrong for a Linux image anyway.
**/node_modules

# Build output. Everything is compiled inside the image.
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/out
backend/generated
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. The image is configured through the environment, never by baking a
# file in. The tracked template is the one exception.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.docker.example

# Test and tooling artifacts
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.eslintcache
**/.turbo

# VCS, editors, OS
.git
.gitignore
**/.github
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Logs and scratch
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.temp
**/.tmp

# Docker's own files -- nothing in the image reads them
**/Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
